WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.706
Learn to estimate perimeter using referents measured in centimetres or metres and

00:00:04.706 --> 00:00:09.587
measure and record perimeter for regular and irregular shapes in cm and m

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:16.582
Estimate the perimeter of a rectangle about 7 cm long and 12 cm wide using the side

00:00:16.582 --> 00:00:22.354
lengths. The answer is 38 cm. Add all four sides once: 2 times (length plus width).

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:28.855
A rectangular school garden measures 13 m by 3 m. How much fencing is needed for all

00:00:28.855 --> 00:00:32.181
four sides? Pause and solve it in your exercise book.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:38.047
The answer is 32 m. 2 times (13 plus 3) equals 32 m.
